---
// Virtual address space (VSS) vs Physical DRAM (RSS) on page fault + Go TCMalloc allocator tiers.
const W = 900;
const H = 304;
---
<figure class="ge5c">
  <div class="ge5c-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Operating system virtual memory lazy page fault mapping into physical RAM alongside Go's mcache, mcentral, and mheap allocator hierarchy.">
      {/* Left panel: OS On-Demand Paging */}
      <rect x="14" y="16" width="424" height="272" rx="10" class="ge5c-card" />
      <text x="30" y="44" class="ge5c-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>1. Virtual Memory (VSS) vs. Physical RAM (RSS)</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>1. Bộ nhớ ảo (VSS) vs. RAM vật lý thật (RSS)</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="64" width="194" height="140" rx="6" class="ge5c-box" />
      <text x="40" y="84" class="ge5c-b">Virtual Space (VSS)</text>
      <rect x="40" y="96" width="174" height="24" rx="4" class="ge5c-cell is-used" />
      <text x="48" y="112" class="ge5c-s">Page 0 (touched → RAM)</text>
      <rect x="40" y="126" width="174" height="24" rx="4" class="ge5c-cell is-idle" />
      <text x="48" y="142" class="ge5c-m">Page 1 (untouched → 0 B)</text>
      <rect x="40" y="156" width="174" height="24" rx="4" class="ge5c-cell is-idle" />
      <text x="48" y="172" class="ge5c-m">Page 2..N (unmapped)</text>

      <line x1="228" y1="108" x2="254" y2="108" class="ge5c-wire-ok" />
      <polygon points="260,108 252,103 252,113" class="ge5c-head-ok" />

      <rect x="264" y="64" width="158" height="140" rx="6" class="ge5c-box is-ok" />
      <text x="276" y="84" class="ge5c-b-ok">Physical RAM (RSS)</text>
      <rect x="276" y="96" width="134" height="32" rx="4" class="ge5c-cell is-used" />
      <text x="284" y="116" class="ge5c-s">4 KiB Frame loaded!</text>
      <text x="276" y="156" class="ge5c-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>First write triggers</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Lần ghi đầu kích hoạt</tspan>
      </text>
      <text x="276" y="172" class="ge5c-b-red">Page Fault (~1–10 µs)</text>

      <rect x="30" y="216" width="392" height="54" rx="6" class="ge5c-box" />
      <text x="42" y="238" class="ge5c-b">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Why mmap(256 MiB) uses ~0.1 MiB RSS initially:</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Tại sao mmap 256 MiB lúc đầu chỉ ăn ~0.1 MiB RSS:</tspan>
      </text>
      <text x="42" y="256" class="ge5c-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>OS allocates RAM lazily only for 4 KiB pages your code touches.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>OS chỉ cấp RAM thật cho từng trang 4 KiB khi code đụng tới.</tspan>
      </text>

      {/* Right panel: Go TCMalloc Hierarchy */}
      <rect x="458" y="16" width="428" height="272" rx="10" class="ge5c-card" />
      <text x="474" y="44" class="ge5c-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>2. Go Heap Allocator Tiers (TCMalloc-style)</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>2. Ba tầng cấp phát Heap của Go (tránh lock)</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="474" y="64" width="396" height="46" rx="6" class="ge5c-box is-ok" />
      <text x="488" y="83" class="ge5c-b-ok">per-P mcache (lock-free fast path)</text>
      <text x="488" y="99" class="ge5c-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>67 size classes (&lt;= 32 KB); noscan skips GC pointer walk</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>67 kích thước (&lt;= 32 KB), không khóa; noscan bỏ qua quét GC</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="474" y="122" width="396" height="46" rx="6" class="ge5c-box" />
      <text x="488" y="141" class="ge5c-b">mcentral (8 KB spans per size class)</text>
      <text x="488" y="157" class="ge5c-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Refills empty mcache spans with fine-grained span locks</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Bơm thêm span 8 KB khi mcache của P hết ô trống</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="474" y="180" width="396" height="46" rx="6" class="ge5c-box is-red" />
      <text x="488" y="199" class="ge5c-b-red">mheap (&gt; 32 KB direct &amp; OS mmap)</text>
      <text x="488" y="215" class="ge5c-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Large objects (&gt; 32 KB) + batched &gt;= 1 MB OS requests</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Object &gt; 32 KB xin thẳng ở đây; gọi OS mmap từng lô &gt;= 1 MB</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="474" y="236" width="396" height="36" rx="6" class="ge5c-box" />
      <text x="488" y="259" class="ge5c-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Releases spare idle spans to Linux via madvise(MADV_DONTNEED)</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Trả RAM rảnh về Linux bằng madvise(MADV_DONTNEED)</tspan>
      </text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Ignore Virtual Set Size (VSS) when hunting RAM leaks: the OS reserves virtual space cheaply, while Go packs small heap allocations in lock-free per-P mcache size classes to avoid OS syscalls.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Đừng hoảng vì chỉ số bộ nhớ ảo VSS: hệ điều hành chỉ cấp RAM vật lý (RSS) theo từng trang 4 KiB khi code đụng vào, còn Go gom biến nhỏ vào mcache theo từng P để khỏi tốn syscall.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .ge5c { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .ge5c-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .ge5c svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .ge5c text { font-size: 12px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .ge5c-card { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .ge5c-box { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .ge5c-box.is-red { stroke: var(--red); fill: var(--red-tint-bg); }
  .ge5c-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge5c-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .ge5c-cell { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .ge5c-cell.is-used { fill: rgba(21, 128, 61, 0.14); stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge5c-cell.is-used { fill: rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.15); stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .ge5c-cell.is-idle { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke-dasharray: 3 3; }
  .ge5c-h { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .ge5c-b { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .ge5c-b-red { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .ge5c-b-ok { font-weight: 700; fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge5c-b-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .ge5c-m { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 11px; }
  .ge5c-s { fill: var(--text); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; }
  .ge5c-wire-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); stroke-width: 2; }
  .ge5c-head-ok { fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge5c-wire-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .ge5c-head-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .ge5c figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
